# Testing

After substantive code changes, run and **read** the output of:

- `pnpm check:fast` (alias: `pnpm check` / `pnpm verify:fast`) for apply loops — unit + patch-coverage; **no** stryker
- Quality phase **B** (`pnpm test:e2e:changed:quiet` + `pnpm stryker:diff`) at agent stages 4/7/9 — not on every loop. Targeted e2e once when green (same target set as CI burn-in). Full `pnpm test:e2e:quiet` / `pnpm test:e2e` / `pnpm verify` only when finish/CI scope needs them; out-of-scope failures per `docs/roadmap/RULES.md` Agent apply hygiene. Flake proof is CI burn-in, not local repeats — local `--repeat-each=3` only if a specific spec failed locally then passed on rerun. Playwright also gates every PR in CI

Also available:

- `pnpm check:integrity` — C1 (openspec-budget, codecov-yml, roadmap) at stage 11 with self-check + stamp
- `pnpm stryker:diff` — changed-line mutations vs `origin/main` (B + CI workflow; not in check:fast)
- `pnpm test:lhci` — Lighthouse CI against `budget.json`
- `pnpm bench` — vitest bench

PBT: use `@fast-check/vitest`; default `numRuns` ~100 locally; CI may raise via `FC_NUM_RUNS`.

Test authorship conventions: skill `write-tests` (mandates in `openspec/config.yaml` quality bar).
